    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Proposition <a href="/tag/D7F67F" data-tag="D7F67F">5.5.4.20</a>, the functor $s$ is fully faithful. A functor $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ belongs to the essential image of $s$ if and only if $f$ has a right adjoint $g$ which factors through $\tau _{\leq n} \calC $. Since $g$ preserves limits, it automatically carries $\calD = \tau _{\leq n} \calD $ into $\tau _{\leq n} \calC $ (Proposition <a href="/tag/645CF2" data-tag="645CF2">5.5.6.16</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
